Total Rewards Academics Florida State offers leading undergraduate, graduate and professional programs, many of which consistently rank among the nation’s top twenty-ﬁve public universities. FSU oﬀers nearly 300 degree programs ranging from Bachelor’s through the Professional level, including Law and Medicine. Read More Accreditation Florida State University is accredited by the Commission on Colleges of the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools (SACSCOC). SACSCOC Accreditation Additionally, many of our colleges and programs hold accreditation through accrediting agencies or governing bodies. Department/Program Accreditation Rankings Florida State is ranked in the Top 20 among national public universities in U.S. News & World Report’s “Best Colleges” guidebook. FSU also holds the Carnegie Commission classification of “Doctoral Universities: Highest Research Activity,” and is designated a Preeminent University by the State of Florida. Read More Office of the Provost Faculty Development & Advancement Faculty Honors & Awards Office of Institutional Research Center for the Advancement of Teaching Research & Creative Activity For assistance with the online application, or for any other questions, please see the Applicant Resources section below or call the FSU Human Resources department at (850) 644-6034. For hands-on assistance, visit our office to use a computer kiosk at University Center A, Suite 6200. Please notify the Human Resources, Equal Opportunity Compliance & Engagement Office (EOCE) at 850-645-1458 or HR-ADA@fsu.edu in advance if you require an ADA disability-related reasonable accommodation(s) to participate in the application process. APPLICANT RESOURCES How to Apply Frequently Asked Questions Technical Resources Application Help How to Clear Your Cache Background Checks Clery Act & Crime Reporting Labor Condition Filing Notices Office of Human Resources 282 Champions Way A6200 University Center Tallahassee, Florida 32306 Phone: (850) 644-6034 Fax: (